 "headline": "On 200 labelled synthetic images, Drishyam at a 30% pixel cap found 0.48 of ground-truth boxes using 0.25 of the image's pixels, versus 0.55 for 20%-overlap 512-px tiling using 1.67: 0.88x its recall (0.75x with one-box-per-class boxes, 1.25x with as-specified mixed boxes) at 0.15x its pixels, which does not meet the 0.9x-at-0.3x hypothesis. It is 0.97x a single 1024-px downscale (0.50 at 0.25 of the pixels), 0.87x L1 tiling (0.55 at 0.50, the best grid) and 1.09x L2 tiling (0.44 at 0.06), and 0.93x L0 tiling when a match needs IoU >= 0.3 (no contains-the-centre clause)."
